#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:5
#: da6c92b141b84c9e963d0353e1c8129b
msgid "Loading the Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:7
#: 86edab6069894ea5b005dd58a5985fb7
msgid "Before loading Firmware, you need to choose which :ref:`autopilot hardware <common-autopilots>` to use. All supported autopilots are suitable for use with AntennaTracker. The antenna tracker firmware can be loaded from the Mission Planner's **Setup \\| Install Firmware** very :ref:`much like any other vehicle <common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk>` if ArduPilot firmware is already loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:15
#: 6698a4515f604a5e87f01cff056c06b0
msgid "Connect the flight control board to the computer using the mini USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:16
#: f01c1e941e19413f9eeda07c72a66849
msgid "Select the appropriate COM port on the top right of the screen but do not push the Connect button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:18
#: 04ed0e9836af43d6ac2cac97bf01b8db
msgid "From the **Initial Setup \\| Install Firmware** page click on the \"Antenna Tracker\" icon on the bottom left.  Follow any instructions that appear and after a minute or so the firmware should be uploaded and you should be able to connect with the mission planner and see the Flight Data screen's HUD update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:24
#: 7fc131dc8fd146608d28cb345f0f1f6c
msgid "If non-ArduPilot firmware is loaded on the autopilot, see :ref:`these instructions <common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>` for instructions to download a version of antennatracker_with_bl.hex firmware and install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loading-the-firmware.rst:28
#: 71bfa5d9b488448b947e65b4b027e337
msgid "Because the EEPROM format is different between the Antenna Tracker firmware and any flight controller software that was previously installed on the board (i.e. Copter or Plane) it is likely the EEPROM will have been erased by the firmware upload."
msgstr ""
